          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            By
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Toposes
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Toposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                are
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
                of toposes.
          %blockquote
            %p
              (In parts of the literature this is denoted merely “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              ”, but that clashes with the common notation for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} the category of
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
          %p
            This is naturally a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+transformations"} geometric transformations
          %p
            That is, a 2-morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo →
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\to g
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* \to g^*
            (which is, by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mate"} mate
            calculus, equivalent to a natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_* \to f_*
            between
            = succeed "s)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
          %p
            Thus,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Toposes
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Toposes
            is equivalent to both of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the (non-full)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-2-category"} sub-2-category
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+2-category"} 1-opposite
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat^{op}
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                on categories that are sheaf toposes and morphisms that are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
                parts of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
            %li
              %p
                the (non-full) sub-2-category of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+2-category"} 2-opposite
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi co
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat^{co}
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                on categories that are sheaf toposes and morphisms that are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
                parts of geometric morphisms.
          %p
          #ElementaryToposesAndLogicalFunctors.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (elementary toposes and logical functors)
              We obtain a very different 2-category of toposes if we take objects to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+toposes"} elementary toposes
              and morphisms the
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logical+functors"} logical functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Log
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Log
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi LogTopos
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LogTopos
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#from_topological_spaces_to_toposes From topological spaces to toposes
          %p
            The operation of forming
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+sheaves"} categories of sheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Top
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Topos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh(-) \,\colon\, Top \longrightarrow Topos
          %p
            embeds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            into toposes. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(f)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh(f)
                  \\,\colon\,
                  Sh(X)
                  \\stackrel{\overset{f^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{f_*}{\to}}
                  Sh(Y)
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
          %p
            Strictly speaking, this functor is not an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
            if we consider
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            as a 1-category and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Toposes
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Toposes
            as a 2-category, since it is then not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
            in the 2-categorical sense—there can be nontrivial 2-cells between geometric morphisms between toposes of sheaves on topological spaces.
          %p
            However, if we regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%281%2C2%29-category"} (1,2)-category
            where the 2-cells are inequalities in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/specialization+ordering"} specialization ordering
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SobTop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SobTop
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+spaces"} sober spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SobTop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SobTop
            to the entire category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
            (which can be viewed as “Grothendieck 0-toposes”).
          %h3#from_toposes_to_higher_toposes From toposes to higher toposes
          %p
            There are similar full embeddings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Topos
                  %mo ↪
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Topos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos \hookrightarrow 2 Topos
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Topos
                  %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Topos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos \hookrightarrow (n,1)Topos
            of sheaf (1-)toposes into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaf"} 2-sheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-toposes"} 2-toposes
            and sheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-toposes"} (n,1)-toposes
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\le n\le \infty
          %p
            Note that these embeddings are
            %em not
            the identity functor on underlying categories: a 1-topos is not itself an
            = succeed "-topos," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            for it.
          %h3#AdjunctionToLocallyPresentable From locally presentable categories to toposes
          %p
            There is a canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi Topos
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U : Topos \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PrCat"} LocPrCat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{op}
            assigning
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-adjunction"} right 2-adjoint
            (
            %a{:href => "#BungeCarboni95"}> Bunge &amp; Carboni 1995 p 235
            ).
          %h3#Limits Limits and colimits
          %p
            The 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Topos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos
            is not all that well-endowed with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
            are finitely complete
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} as 2-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ShTopos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ShTopos
            is closed under finite limits in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Topos
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos/Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ShToposes
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ShToposes
            is the topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq Sh(*)
          %h4#Colimits Colimits
          %p The supply with colimits is better:
          #ColimitsByInverseImageLimits.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              All small (indexed)
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-colimit"} 2-colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ShTopos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ShTopos
              exists and are computed as (indexed)
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limit"} 2-limit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              of the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              functors.
          %p
            This appears as
            %a{:href => "#Moerdijk"} Moerdijk, theorem 2.5
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℱ
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ℰ
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ℰ
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{F} &amp;\stackrel{p_2}{\to}&amp; \mathcal{E}_2
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{p_1}}\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f_2}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{E}_1 &amp;\underset{f_1}{\to}&amp; \mathcal{E}
                    }
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-pullback"} 2-pullback
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1, f_2
                  are both
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudomonic+morphism"} pseudomonic morphism
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %msub
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mn 2
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_1 \coprod \mathcal{E}_2 \to \mathcal{E}
                  is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
            %p
              then the diagram of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℱ
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 2
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ℰ
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi p
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mn 2
                                    %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ℰ
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{F} &amp;\stackrel{p_2^*}{\leftarrow}&amp; \mathcal{E}_2
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{p_1^*}}\uparrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \uparrow^{\mathrlap{f_2^*}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{E}_1 &amp;\underset{f_1^*}{\leftarrow}&amp; \mathcal{E}
                    }
            %p
              is a 2-pullback in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              and so by the
              %a{:href => "#ColimitsByInverseImageLimits"} above
              the original square is also a 2-pushout.
          %p
            This appears as theorem 5.1 in (
            %a{:href => "#BungeLack"}> BungeLack
            )
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
          %p
            This is in (
            %a{:href => "#BungeLack"}> BungeLack, proposition 4.3
            ).
          %h4#Products Products
          %p
          #ProductOfGrothendieckToposes.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+toposes"} presheaf toposes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C_i)
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos
              is the presheaf topos on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
              of their sites:
            #eq:ToposProductOfPresheafToposes.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Topos
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Cat
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PSh(C_1)
                    \\times_{Topos}
                    PSh(C_2)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    PSh(C_1 \times_{Cat} C_2 )
                    \\,.
            %p
              More generally, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_i
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos
              of the sheaf topos is the sheaf topos over the product site
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C_1 \times C_2, J_1 \times J_2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_1 \times J_2
              is the Grothendieck topology on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
              generated from products of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+sieves"} covering sieves
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_1
              and
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_2
            #eq:ToposProductOfSheafToposes.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Topos
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh(C_1, J_1)
                    \\times_{Topos}
                    PSh(C_2, J_2)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    PSh(C_1 \times C_2,\,  J_1 \times J_2 )
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            (cf.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Pitts85"} Pitts 1985 proof of Thm. 2.3
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Valero18"} Valero 2018 p 98-99
          %p
          #ProofOfProductOfGrothendieckToposes.proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Since every sheaf topos admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              that has all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ToposProductOfPresheafToposes"} (1)
              under the assumption that the sites
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_i
              have all finite limits. (We refer to these small categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_i
              as “sites” already, even though in the presheaf case they are as such equipped with the trivial
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            %p
              To check the defining
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒳
                    %mo ↔
                    %mi 𝒴
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_\ast \,\colon\,
                    \\mathcal{X}
                    \\leftrightarrow
                    \\mathcal{Y}
                    \\,\colon\,
                    f^\ast
            %p
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes
              (generally between
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserving
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocontinuous+functors"} cocontinuous functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %mi 𝒴
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{X} \overset{f^\ast}{\longleftarrow} \mathcal{Y}
            %p
              (by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "adjoint+functor+theorem#StatementForLocPresCategories"} for locally presentable categories
            %p Then writing
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_i
                    \\,\colon\,
                    C_1 \times C_2
                    \\longrightarrow
                    C_i
            %p
              for the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              functors out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
              of the given sites, and writing
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p^\ast_i
                    \\,\colon\,
                    PSh(C_i)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    PSh( C_1 \times C_2 )
            %p
              for the corresponding pre-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              functors on presheaves (which presverve all (co)limits since (co)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits+of+presheaves+are+computed+objectwise"}> limits of presheaves are computed objectwise
              ), it is sufficient to show that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Topos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X} \in Topos
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒳
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^\ast_i
                    \\,\colon\,
                    PSh(C_i) \longrightarrow \mathcal{X}
                    \\,,
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    i \in \{1,2\}
            %p
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of cocontinuous and finitely continuous functors, there is a unique such functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f_1, f_2)^\ast \,\colon\,
                    PSh(C_1 \times C_2) \longrightarrow \mathcal{X}
            %p
              which makes the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commute
            %svg{:height => "157.197pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 347.568 157.197", :width => "347.568pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
              %defs
                %g
                  %symbol{:id => "eE8jF-j0qXWSwFFhzoP7tsGKsgw=-glyph0-0", :overflow => "visible"}
